    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Where the code is generated:** `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` computes the code just before persisting, via a new helper:\n\n```java\nprivate String nextCustomerCode(String lastName) {\n    String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase(java.util.Locale.ROOT);\n    int sequence = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().size() + 1;\n    return String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence);\n}\n```\n\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (`\"smithers\"` \u2192 `SMI`), guarded for names shorter than 3.\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count, so consecutive creates increment (`SMI-000N`, then `JON-000(N+1)`), satisfying the test's `cb == ca + 1` assertion.\n\n**Supporting changes to plumb the field through:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 new persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (tests run on hsqldb; the rest kept consistent).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0) \u2014 that acceptance class is the only concrete test in the repo.",
